# Local reference installation. Use your HTTPS origin behind a trusted proxy when hosted.
APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
HOST=127.0.0.1
PORT=3000
DATA_DIR=.boopity
# A persistent authentication secret is generated in DATA_DIR/auth-secret if none is supplied.
# A separate DATA_DIR/settings-key encrypts saved provider credentials. Preserve both keys.
# Never commit secrets or copy preview credentials. Use the setup UI for email/Google settings.
# Optional: set BOOPITY_SETUP_PASSWORD privately to 15–128 characters before startup.
# It opens unfinished setup without email and stops working once the owner is verified.
# Never use a VITE_ prefix. No sample password is supplied. Remove this setting after owner verification.
# Without it, startup opens/prints a private Finish setup link; choose a password in Your account.
# Changing a host password and restarting resets setup access. An unchanged host password
# does not undo a newer password saved in the wizard. It cannot reopen a claimed installation.
# Keep startup logs private. Optional: BOOPITY_SETUP_LINK=manual suppresses automatic links;
# then run `npm run manage -- setup-link` in a private console with the same configuration.
# Optional: BOOPITY_OPEN_BROWSER=false disables automatic browser opening.
# Installer-managed email (optional, fresh installations only): BOOPITY_OWNER_EMAIL
# pins the intended owner before public access. With host-configured email delivery,
# that owner can verify a code and claim in the browser without a console token.
# Without working host-configured email, this path stays locked. This is NOT an
# email-provider provisioner. Hosting and email accounts belong to the installer.
# Never expose the owner email, mail credentials, codes or setup tokens via VITE_ variables.
# Legacy host-code setup: supply a NEW strong random BOOPITY_SETUP_TOKEN via host secrets.
# This disables automatic links. Use /setup/code; see INSTALLER-ACCESS.md.
# Recovery: BOOPITY_RECOVERY_TOKEN, for an already claimed installation only.
# Tokens expire in 30 minutes; remove their environment variables after use. Never reuse them.
# See SELF-HOSTING.md for complete email/Google environment-group overrides and recovery.
# Hosted installations must set APP_URL to their exact public HTTPS origin.
# Platform-supplied URLs are not detected automatically. No hosting adapter is needed.
# Do not add VITE_ prefixed secrets; those would be exposed in the client bundle.
# Optional Stripe overrides: supply a complete pair through the host's secret store.
# BOOPITY_STRIPE_TEST_KEY and BOOPITY_STRIPE_TEST_WEBHOOK_SECRET
# BOOPITY_STRIPE_LIVE_KEY and BOOPITY_STRIPE_LIVE_WEBHOOK_SECRET
# Only restricted rk_test_/rk_live_ keys are accepted. Never add real values to this example.
# Either member makes that mode host-managed. Incomplete pairs fail closed; restart after changes.
# Verify account + signed destination and enable checkout in Payments & integrations.
# Old SaaS STRIPE_SECRET_KEY / STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET / recurring prices are not reused.
